[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3867632358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-3867632358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":3867632358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mh2Lm","user":{"login":"viksl","id":33526847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNTI2ODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33526847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl","html_url":"https://github.com/viksl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T17:14:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T17:17:44Z","body":"I can confirm this from the included mrp (both the engine cube as well as the car meshes) - win 11, rtx4070, intel i5 13600kf, godot 4.6 stable.\n\nThere was a major rework of the SSR in 4.6 so maybe @blueskythlikesclouds would know something?\n\nProbably doesn't matter but when I move the sidebar in the editor it looks like this:\n\n<img width=\"1022\" height=\"770\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/616af8bc-c078-42fe-91de-f5b25d746c7e\" />\n\nAgain, I don't know if it's an issue or not, just wanted to include it in case it mattered.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3867632358/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870070585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-3870070585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":3870070585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mrJc5","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T08:24:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T08:25:24Z","body":"These are a consequence of SSR in general. I tried to reduce it as much as possible, but after some point it's not possible to handle all cases without the user adjusting the \"Depth Tolerance\" value in a per-scene basis.\n\nTry playing around with the sample count and depth tolerance values and see if it helps.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870070585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870298375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-3870298375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":3870298375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7msBEH","user":{"login":"viksl","id":33526847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNTI2ODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33526847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl","html_url":"https://github.com/viksl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viksl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T09:01:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T09:19:33Z","body":"> These are a consequence of SSR in general. I tried to reduce it as much as possible, but after some point it's not possible to handle all cases without the user adjusting the \"Depth Tolerance\" value in a per-scene basis.\n> \n> Try playing around with the sample count and depth tolerance values and see if it helps.\n\nHm, I tried it and I don't think you can solve it with these two settings (by max sample count, you meant the max steps, correct?). It seems the Tolerance having only one decimal is sort of really limiting here. At 0 the reflections break while at 0.1 you start getting the issues quite a bit already.\n\nIs this on purpose, are smaller values/differences for the depth tolerance not a thing?\n\nBut then again i'm not familiar with SSR that much so my feedback here is pretty limited.\n\nBtw, in this picture:\n\n<img width=\"745\" height=\"694\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e920c02-ebef-45a6-bc5c-e18c00e22d6f\" />\n\nThe reflections are starting to create a \"column\" or getting connected to the object which is a fair bit above the ground. Is that a normal part of SSR? I assume that's normal but just wanted to ask.\n\nAt dept tolerance the reflections don't have the streaks reported by the OP, or it might be better to say the streaking is now across the entire reflection but the reflection does not appear away from where you would expect the reflections to be as below. \n\n<img width=\"731\" height=\"477\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f36ee45-aaf3-4284-8b41-c5db4ca2ecb6\" />\n\nI assume these are limits of SSR in Godot for not?\n\nAnyway, I wonder if an option to have more subtler depth tolerance changes would help to mitigate these issues better?\n\nAlso, while I'm on those depth values. Apart from being limited to one decimal, the range seems pretty massive considering how much of a difference going from 0 -> 0.1 -> 0.2 makes, the maximum is 128 (I guess for som large distances you need larger value or something?).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870298375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871780205","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-3871780205","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":3871780205,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mxq1t","user":{"login":"coyotezin","id":24484602,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDg0NjAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24484602?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin","html_url":"https://github.com/coyotezin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coyotezin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T13:40:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:40:41Z","body":"At 0 depth tolerance it does seem to help mitigate the vertical streaks but yeah it does ruin the reflections as @viksl stated.\n\n<img width=\"1126\" height=\"752\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a320f155-c61a-4026-82ff-5413d6990025\" />\n\nIncreasing Max Steps after setting Depth Tolerance at 0 only make things worse since you get to see even more broken reflections.\n\nIm currently making a racing game and reflections are super important for car games in general, i've tried a few different workarounds using ReflectionProbe but i could not find an ideal way to use it for proper car body panel reflections since ReflectionProbe would also show up a lot of \"impossible reflections\" of things that are behind a panel for example, besides that, it causes other visual issues in general.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871780205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4448621694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-4448621694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":4448621694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCSiUfg","user":{"login":"KnIfER","id":11593903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTkzOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11593903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER","html_url":"https://github.com/KnIfER","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnIfER/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T07:28:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T07:30:12Z","body":"Anti aliasing contributes to this SSR problem :   \n\n- Anti alias off\n\n<img width=\"649\" height=\"338\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64dde860-fc47-47c0-ac24-9380892eefbe\" />\n\n- Anti alias on ( msaa 3d ) \n\n<img width=\"625\" height=\"310\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5cb40fa7-bf5a-4c0d-a5cb-b88c671b62c9\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4448621694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024307416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-5024307416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":5024307416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK3jY2A","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-20T15:59:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T15:59:24Z","body":"> Is this on purpose, are smaller values/differences for the depth tolerance not a thing?\n\nThere's no technical limitation for using more precise values, it's just how it's configured in the inspector. In the meantime, you can set a more precise value through a script:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t$WorldEnvironment.environment.ssr_depth_tolerance = 0.05\n```\n\nI wonder what happens if you set a slightly random value each frame and enable TAA or FSR2 to benefit from some jittering...\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\t$WorldEnvironment.environment.ssr_depth_tolerance = randf_range(0.04, 0.08)\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024307416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6265135598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-6265135598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":6265135598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdW5h7g","user":{"login":"DeskGoblin","id":191428251,"node_id":"U_kgDOC2j2mw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191428251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin","html_url":"https://github.com/DeskGoblin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T10:29:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T10:29:35Z","body":"Bump. Still an issue as of Godot 4.8 Dev 6. Furthermore I get this sort of wavy effect when reducing depth tolerance to zero.\n\nDepth Tolerance 0.5 (default)\n<img width=\"653\" height=\"835\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f01bcb7e-9ae4-40ed-ad24-314b64b92845\" />\n\nDepth Tolerance 0.0 \n<img width=\"794\" height=\"795\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ea48961-20fe-46d4-b020-6d5430029c90\" />\n\nLooks even worse with anti aliasing turned off.\n<img width=\"664\" height=\"811\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51bc317d-4a2d-4938-bd78-38100e9dbbe9\" />\n\nI could probably let it slide if it weren't for the fact that changing camera pitch causes noticeable jitter. Seems to be even worse at near distances.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d745cb9-7043-422f-bd7e-293deccb0867\n\nOn a separate note the reflection cutoff in the beginning is a bit strange, and happens quite often. Anyone know how I can correct it?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6265135598/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6268123929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116008#issuecomment-6268123929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116008","id":6268123929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdZv7GQ","user":{"login":"DeskGoblin","id":191428251,"node_id":"U_kgDOC2j2mw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191428251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin","html_url":"https://github.com/DeskGoblin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeskGoblin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T13:16:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T13:16:07Z","body":"Follow-up. Turning off TAA revealed this scaling effect. The following recordings are with all AA off.\n\nDepth tolerance at zero:\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62c6bb70-2022-4bcf-a49f-e53450226349\n\nDepth tolerance at 0.5 (default):\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b52d103-e902-43e8-b0b0-392130164bae","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6268123929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]